hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15892","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, he said: I heard Bushayr ibn Yasar, he said: I heard Suwayd ibn al-Numan, a man of the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, of the companions of the tree, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was on a journey and they had no food. He said: Sawiq was brought, and they chewed from it and drank from it. Then water was brought and they rinsed. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood and prayed."
"15893","Ibn Numayr narrated to us: Yahya narrated to us, from Bushayr ibn Yasar, from Suwayd ibn al-Numan, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the year of Khaybar, until when we were at al-Sahba and he prayed Asr, he called for foods, and nothing was brought but sawiq. They ate and drank from it. Then he stood for Maghrib and rinsed, and we rinsed with him, and he did not touch water."
